+// wwe2k14 patch (Session 7c, CAUSES): gpu_anatomy_gpu_marks_mode 1 (sparse marks) and the rows_covered column.
+// Measurement only, like the marks themselves.
+// Mode 1 marks a draw (pre + post, as mode 0) only if something was recorded for it since the last mark that
+// ended a row (CausesEventSum changed: an upload, a texture load, a dispatch, a barrier batch, a render pass begin,
+// a pipeline bind or creation). Every resolve keeps its before / after marks. A draw that isn't marked and has no
+// event leaves its time in a block, which ends at the next mark of any kind; to keep a marked draw's preparation
+// free of the unmarked draws before it, an unmarked row's end arms the deferred command buffer's event hook, and the
+// first event command recorded after it gets a prep_begin mark right before it (GpuMarksSparseBeforeEvent). After
+// gpu_anatomy_gpu_marks_every rows without a mark, an event-free draw gets a block mark after its draw call.
